    "https://jobs.uc.edu/job/Instructor-Asst-Prof-Research%2C-College-of-Medicine%2C-Dept-of-Pharmacology%2C-Physiology%2C-Neurobiology/103472-en_US": {
      "title": "Instructor / Asst Prof Research, College of Medicine, Dept of Pharmacology, Physiology, Neurobiology",
      "description": "Instructor / Asst Prof Research, College of Medicine, Dept of Pharmacology, Physiology, Neurobiology Job Details | University of Cincinnati Skip to main content Language English (United States) Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Language English (United States) Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Menu Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Job Title: Instructor / Asst Prof Research, College of Medicine, Dept of Pharmacology, Physiology, Neurobiology Posting Start Date: 9/22/26 Work Arrangement: Onsite Current UC employees must apply internally via SuccessFactors Faculty rank and compensation will be based on experience and academic credentials. Next Lives at the University of Cincinnati Founded in 1819, the University of Cincinnati ranks among the nation’s best urban public research universities. Home to more than 53,600 students, 12,000 faculty and staff, and over 360,000 living alumni, UC, a Carnegie 1 institution, combines research prowess with a physical setting The New York Times has called “the most ambitious campus design program in the country.\" UC's momentum has never been stronger as the anchor of the Cincinnati Innovation District, the oldest cooperative education (co-op) program in the country with students earning $94 million annually through paid experiences, an academic health system, and as a member of the Big 12 Conference. The university contributes $10.6 billion in economic impact to the city and $22.7 billion to the state of Ohio. At UC, next is all of us. Learn more at uc.edu . UC is a mission-driven organization where we are committed to student success and positively transforming the community through scholarship and service.  We thrive on innovation, making an impact, and fostering an environment where staff and faculty are key contributors to UC’s success. Job Overview Founded in 1819, the University of Cincinnati puts education into action, ranking among the nation’s best urban public research universities. Home to more than 53,000 students, 10,500 faculty and staff and 330,000 alumni, UC combines a Top 35 research university with a physical setting The New York Times calls “the most ambitious campus design program in the country.” With the launch of Next Lives Here, the Cincinnati Innovation District, a $100 million JobsOhio investment, worldwide leadership in cooperative education, a dynamic academic health center and entry into the Big 12 athletic conference, UC’s momentum has never been stronger. UC’s annual budget tops $1.6 billion and its endowment totals $1.8 billion. At UC, today’s possibilities spark tomorrow’s reality. As one of the oldest medical schools in the country, the UC College of Medicine has a reputation for training best-in-class health care professionals and developing cutting-edge procedures and research that improve the health and clinical care of patients. The College of Medicine, Department of Pharmacology, Physiology, and Neurobiology is recruiting a Research Instructor with the potential to hire a Research Assistant Professor. A Research Instructor/Assistant Professor at the University of Cincinnati is expected to teach, have interest in productive scholarship and willingness to collaborate with students and faculty for the betterment of the University, conduct research, scholarly and other professional activities. This position will support the University of Cincinnati’s mission and commitment to excellence in our students, faculty, staff, and all our activities. Essential Functions Conduct original research that advances the discipline, including designing studies, collecting/analyzing data, and producing scholarly outputs. Publish in peer‑reviewed journals, present at conferences, and contribute to the broader scholarly community. Prepare and submit grant proposals to secure external funding; manage awarded grants, budgets, compliance, and reporting. Supervise research personnel, including graduate students, undergraduate research assistants, and postdoctoral scholars. Maintain an active, independent research agenda aligned with departmental priorities and disciplinary standards. Deliver high‑quality instruction in assigned courses (undergraduate or graduate), including lectures, labs, seminars, or independent study supervision. Prepare course materials, syllabi, assessments, and learning activities aligned with current disciplinary knowledge. Assess student performance using appropriate methods and provide timely feedback. Hold office hours and advise students, including mentoring research students and guiding academic/career development. Supervise theses, dissertations, or capstone research, depending on departmental needs. Participate in departmental committees, faculty meetings, and academic governance. Contribute to curriculum development, program review, or accreditation activities when relevant. Provide disciplinary expertise through peer review of manuscripts, grant proposals, or conference organization. Engage in community or professional outreach, such as workshops, invited talks, or collaborations. Communicate effectively in writing and speech, including complex concepts. Meet deadlines, manage multiple projects, and prioritize tasks. Collaborate with colleagues, attend meetings, and contribute to a positive academic environment. Understand and apply university policies, compliance requirements, and ethical standards. Required Education Must have obtained a Doctorate or terminal degree from a regionally accredited college or university of recognized standing in a field appropriate to the requirements of the position. Research Instructor Considerable professional work experience in the given field. Ability to present complex material to students unfamiliar with a subject. Outstanding writing skills to present research in written format. Possess exceptional communication skills and the ability to work and collaborate with individuals from a variety of backgrounds. - OR - Research Assistant Professor Demonstrated excellence in research evidenced by strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals. Candidates for a research-track appointment should demonstrate intellectual leadership and impact on the field and potential significant contributions to the department, University of Cincinnati, and wider scholarly community. Additional Qualifications Considered Able to work independently with minimal direction Mentoring experience of undergraduate and graduate students Formal grant writing training, preferably with a track record of grant funding as principal investigator. Published as first and/or senior author in discipline-leading journals. Experience working with rodents in preclinical research Physical Requirements/Work Environment Office environment/no specific unusual physical or environmental demands. Compensation and Benefits UC offers an exceptional benefits package designed to support your well-being, financial security, and work-life balance. (UC Benefits) Eligibility may vary by position and FTE status. Highlights include: Salary Information: Comprehensive Tuition Remission UC provides tuition remission for you and your eligible dependents, covering tuition costs for nearly all undergraduate and graduate programs offered by the university. Robust Retirement Plans As a UC employee, you won’t contribute to Social Security (except Medicare). Instead, you’ll choose between state pension plans (OPERS, STRS) or an Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP), with UC contributing 14–18% of your salary based on position. Real Work-Life Balance UC prioritizes work-life balance with a generous time-off policy, including: Vacation and sick time 11 paid holidays and additional end-of-year paid time off (Winter Season Days) 6 weeks of paid parental leave for new parents Additional Benefits Include: Competitive salary based on experience Comprehensive health coverage (medical, dental, vision, prescription) Flexible spending accounts & wellness programs Professional development & mentorship opportunities To learn more about why UC is a great place to work, please visit our Careers Page . UC is an E-Verify employer.  If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. Click here for a list of acceptable documents. Important : To apply you must create a profile and submit a complete job application through the UC applicant portal . We are unable to consider “easy apply” applications submitted via other websites. For questions about the UC recruiting process or to request accommodations with the application, please contact UC HR at jobs@uc.edu . **FOR ALL FACULTY HIRES OFFICIAL ACADEMIC TRANSCRIPTS WILL BE REQUIRED AT THE TIME OF HIRE Equal Opportunity Employer.  Building a workplace where all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment, including Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans. REQ: 103472 Apply now Clery and HEOA Notice Notice of Non-Discrimination eAccessibility Concern Privacy Statement University of Cincinnati | 2600 Clifton Ave. | Cincinnati, OH 45221 | ph: 513-556-6000"
    },
    "https://jobs.uc.edu/job/Instructor-Adjunct%2C-College-of-Nursing/104180-en_US": {
      "title": "Instructor - Adjunct, College of Nursing",
      "description": "Instructor - Adjunct, College of Nursing Job Details | University of Cincinnati Skip to main content Language English (United States) Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Language English (United States) Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Menu Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Job Title: Instructor - Adjunct, College of Nursing Posting Start Date: 9/22/26 Work Arrangement: Onsite Current UC employees must apply internally via SuccessFactors You are invited to apply to be considered for one of multiple vacancies of the same position.  The number of positions varies depending on the needs of the department. Rank and compensation will be based on experience and academic credentials. Next Lives at the University of Cincinnati Founded in 1819, the University of Cincinnati ranks among the nation’s best urban public research universities. Home to more than 53,600 students, 12,000 faculty and staff, and over 360,000 living alumni, UC, a Carnegie 1 institution, combines research prowess with a physical setting The New York Times has called “the most ambitious campus design program in the country.\" UC's momentum has never been stronger as the anchor of the Cincinnati Innovation District, the oldest cooperative education (co-op) program in the country with students earning $94 million annually through paid experiences, an academic health system, and as a member of the Big 12 Conference. The university contributes $10.6 billion in economic impact to the city and $22.7 billion to the state of Ohio. At UC, next is all of us. Learn more at uc.edu . UC is a mission-driven organization where we are committed to student success and positively transforming the community through scholarship and service.  We thrive on innovation, making an impact, and fostering an environment where staff and faculty are key contributors to UC’s success. Job Overview This position is for in-person facility based clinical rotation. On a part-time limited basis, the Adjunct Faculty member’s primary academic functions include teaching, discovering, creating, and reporting knowledge to students. Adjunct faculty members will be expected to (1) use our course management system (Canvas) and any textbook-specific systems; (2) hold regular office hours to meet with students and reply to student communications in a timely manner. Essential Functions On a part-time basis, conduct and teach assigned undergraduate and/or graduate-level courses and seminars. May serve as an academic advisor for students and evaluate student coursework. Engage in other activities ancillary to or in support of responsibilities. Review, and where necessary, respond in a timely manner to all University-related communications. Other related duties as assigned. Minimum Requirements A BSN or higher from an approved registered nursing education program Required Trainings/Certifications Current, valid licensure as a registered nurse in Ohio Required Experience Have at least two (2) years of experience in the practice of nursing as a registered nurse. MSN required for accelerated program program instructors. BSN required for undergraduate clinical instructors. May need current BLS/CPR and immunization verification per facility guidelines. Required Education A BSN or higher from an approved registered nursing education program Required Trainings/Certifications Current, valid licensure as a registered nurse in Ohio Required Experience Have at least two (2) years of experience in the practice of nursing as a registered nurse. Compensation and Benefits UC offers an exceptional benefits package designed to support your well-being, financial security, and work-life balance. (UC Benefits) Eligibility may vary by position and FTE status. Highlights include: Comprehensive Tuition Remission UC provides tuition remission for you and your eligible dependents, covering tuition costs for nearly all undergraduate and graduate programs offered by the university. Robust Retirement Plans As a UC employee, you won’t contribute to Social Security (except Medicare). Instead, you’ll choose between state pension plans (OPERS, STRS) or an Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP), with UC contributing 14–18% of your salary based on position. Real Work-Life Balance UC prioritizes work-life balance with a generous time-off policy, including: Vacation and sick time 11 paid holidays and additional end-of-year paid time off (Winter Season Days) 6 weeks of paid parental leave for new parents Additional Benefits Include: Competitive salary based on experience Comprehensive health coverage (medical, dental, vision, prescription) Flexible spending accounts & wellness programs Professional development & mentorship opportunities To learn more about why UC is a great place to work, please visit our Careers Page . UC is an E-Verify employer.  If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. Click here for a list of acceptable documents. Important : To apply you must create a profile and submit a complete job application through the UC applicant portal . We are unable to consider “easy apply” applications submitted via other websites. For questions about the UC recruiting process or to request accommodations with the application, please contact UC HR at jobs@uc.edu . **FOR ALL FACULTY HIRES OFFICIAL ACADEMIC TRANSCRIPTS WILL BE REQUIRED AT THE TIME OF HIRE Equal Opportunity Employer.  Building a workplace where all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment, including Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans. REQ: 104180 Apply now Clery and HEOA Notice Notice of Non-Discrimination eAccessibility Concern Privacy Statement University of Cincinnati | 2600 Clifton Ave. | Cincinnati, OH 45221 | ph: 513-556-6000"
    },
    "https://jobs.uc.edu/job/Psychiatrist%2C-Assistant-Professor%2C-Psychiatry-&-Behavioral-Neuroscience/104173-en_US": {
      "title": "Psychiatrist, Assistant Professor, Psychiatry & Behavioral Neuroscience",
      "description": "Psychiatrist, Assistant Professor, Psychiatry & Behavioral Neuroscience Job Details | University of Cincinnati Skip to main content Language English (United States) Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Language English (United States) Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Sign In To My Profile Employee Login Menu Search Jobs Sign in or Create Account FAQ Why Choose UC Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Job Title: Psychiatrist, Assistant Professor, Psychiatry & Behavioral Neuroscience Posting Start Date: 9/22/26 Work Arrangement: Onsite Current UC employees must apply internally via SuccessFactors Faculty rank and compensation will be based on experience and academic credentials. Next Lives at the University of Cincinnati Founded in 1819, the University of Cincinnati ranks among the nation’s best urban public research universities. Home to more than 53,600 students, 12,000 faculty and staff, and over 360,000 living alumni, UC, a Carnegie 1 institution, combines research prowess with a physical setting The New York Times has called “the most ambitious campus design program in the country.\" UC's momentum has never been stronger as the anchor of the Cincinnati Innovation District, the oldest cooperative education (co-op) program in the country with students earning $94 million annually through paid experiences, an academic health system, and as a member of the Big 12 Conference. The university contributes $10.6 billion in economic impact to the city and $22.7 billion to the state of Ohio. At UC, next is all of us. Learn more at uc.edu . UC is a mission-driven organization where we are committed to student success and positively transforming the community through scholarship and service.  We thrive on innovation, making an impact, and fostering an environment where staff and faculty are key contributors to UC’s success. Job Overview As one of the oldest medical schools in the country, the UC College of Medicine has a reputation for training best-in-class health care professionals and developing cutting-edge procedures and research that improves the health and clinical care of patients. The Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Neuroscience is dedicated to high quality medical student, resident, and fellow education, excellence in patient care, and advancing the science in psychiatry and behavioral neurosciences through clinical trials and ongoing collaborative research. The Freeman Center for Developmental Disabilities offers coordinated, person-centered care for adults with developmental disabilities. Our expert team provides primary care, behavioral health, psychiatry, physical medicine and rehabilitation, nurse care coordination, social work and dietary support in an accessible setting, so patients have coordinated care plans and fewer separate visits. The College of Medicine, Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Neuroscience is recruiting for a Psychiatrist at the Assistant, Associate or Professor level to provide care at the Freeman Center. The final rank and title of the appointment will be commensurate with the experience and professional accomplishments of the selected applicant.  Medical Director and leadership opportunities may be available for qualified candidates. Essential Functions Provide direct patient care in an outpatient setting. Conduct thorough psychiatric evaluations & assessments for new & returning outpatients. Develop & implement individualized treatment plans, including medication management & psychotherapy as appropriate. Provide crisis intervention & stabilization for acute psychiatric conditions presenting in the outpatient setting. Communicate clinical findings, treatment recommendations, and clinically significant changes in patient status to relevant members of the treatment team in accordance with applicable privacy and documentation standards Collaborate with Freeman Center multidisciplinary team members and other referring or treating professionals to coordinate care and support continuity of treatment. Engage in continuous professional development & stay current with advancements in the field of psychiatry. Teach medical students, residents, and fellows. Opportunity for administrative and leadership roles, participation in quality improvement, peer supervision, and formal mentorship. Opportunities for clinical research at various UC Health facilities, hospitals, and other local health care systems. Minimum Requirements Prior to effective date of appointment, must have all of the following: MD/DO or equivalent degree Ohio Medical License Completion of a 4-year Psychiatry residency Additional Qualifications Considered Board eligible/board certified in General Psychiatry Experience providing psychiatric assessment and evidence-based treatment in an outpatient clinical setting. Specialized training or professional experience in the field of developmental psychiatry Demonstrated expertise or substantial clinical experience in the care for individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities and co-occurring psychiatric conditions. Experience working in an academic medical center, hospital-based outpatient practice, or interdisciplinary health care environment. Interest or experience in clinical program development, measurement-based care, quality improvement, education, or collaborative scholarship. Physical Requirements/Work Environment Office environment/no specific unusual physical or environmental demands. Compensation and Benefits UC offers an exceptional benefits package designed to support your well-being, financial security, and work-life balance. (UC Benefits) Eligibility may vary by position and FTE status. Highlights include: Salary Information: Comprehensive Tuition Remission UC provides tuition remission for you and your eligible dependents, covering tuition costs for nearly all undergraduate and graduate programs offered by the university. Robust Retirement Plans As a UC employee, you won’t contribute to Social Security (except Medicare). Instead, you’ll choose between state pension plans (OPERS, STRS) or an Alternative Retirement Plan (ARP), with UC contributing 14–18% of your salary based on position. Real Work-Life Balance UC prioritizes work-life balance with a generous time-off policy, including: Vacation and sick time 11 paid holidays and additional end-of-year paid time off (Winter Season Days) 6 weeks of paid parental leave for new parents Additional Benefits Include: Competitive salary based on experience Comprehensive health coverage (medical, dental, vision, prescription) Flexible spending accounts & wellness programs Professional development & mentorship opportunities To learn more about why UC is a great place to work, please visit our Careers Page . UC is an E-Verify employer.  If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. Click here for a list of acceptable documents. Important : To apply you must create a profile and submit a complete job application through the UC applicant portal . We are unable to consider “easy apply” applications submitted via other websites. For questions about the UC recruiting process or to request accommodations with the application, please contact UC HR at jobs@uc.edu . **FOR ALL FACULTY HIRES OFFICIAL ACADEMIC TRANSCRIPTS WILL BE REQUIRED AT THE TIME OF HIRE Equal Opportunity Employer.  Building a workplace where all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment, including Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans. REQ: 104173 Apply now Clery and HEOA Notice Notice of Non-Discrimination eAccessibility Concern Privacy Statement University of Cincinnati | 2600 Clifton Ave. | Cincinnati, OH 45221 | ph: 513-556-6000"
